    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our primary engine. With a stellar 83.29 efficiency score against Warren, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive +16% park adjustment and a significant platoon edge, making him a locked-in must-start for RBI and run production. Joining him in the top tier of projected output are **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Jackson Merrill** is a particularly intriguing play; despite the high-caliber catcher defense behind the plate, the favorable wind conditions pushing out at the stadium and a strong matchup against Stock elevate his ceiling. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, meanwhile, continues to capitalize on favorable park dimensions and a distinct SP skill advantage against Bassitt, providing a reliable foundation for our 5x5 totals.\n\nStrategic depth remains a point of emphasis today, especially with **Kyle Tucker** (73.93) and **Andy Pages** (72.19) anchoring the middle-order potential despite lineups still being considered \"pending.\" The most difficult decision for the staff was the final bench spot, where **Dominic Smith** (51.11) fell just short of inclusion. While **Dominic Smith** offers a decent floor, he was eclipsed by the higher upside and dynamic platoon positioning of **Wade Meckler** and **Sam Antonacci**. We are monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** closely; the latter remains sidelined on the IL, leaving a significant void in power production that forces our active starters to perform in the high-efficiency zone. We have benched **Luis Lara** (37.20) entirely, as his matchup against Gilbert does not meet our minimum requirement for daily game caps, prioritizing the preservation of our roster for more favorable pitching environments later in the week.",
